		)
		(uuid "02035623-5931-4f87-87af-3e0170a60b0f")
	)
	(text "D4\nMBRS360\nreverse block"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208 122 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0e0c19b1-4af8-4e92-8b08-6f9c8d773edf")
	)
	(text "RETIRED - do NOT fit: floating-supply P-ch (ZD1/R_Z1/C_Z1/LM321, IRF9Z34N) and the\nvoltage-follower TIP122 NPN. See design doc 7A.7."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 188 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2d170289-daf4-419c-a5a9-692bff754154")
	)
	(text "Q1\nTIP147 PNP Darlington\nTO-220 + heatsink\n(or N-MOSFET alt:\nSUP70060E/RFP50N06)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 191 103 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "40cd3371-b258-41fa-8976-eef64d72cb9e")
	)
	(text "ANTI-BRAKE = CONSTANT-CURRENT SOURCE (this revision):\nClassic high-side op-amp current source. GD1 drives Q1 and regulates the drop across\nRsense (0.1 ohm) to equal the demand, holding I = Vdemand/Rsense regardless of motor.\nDemand: a 50kHz MCU PWM, level-shifted (2N2222) and RC-filtered (470n + R) to 0-0.3V.\nPot sets PWM duty -> current. 0% = 0A (off); full = 3A.\nWhy a current source: a stalled motor (start line) is ~short; a voltage source would\ndump unbounded current. A current source bounds it to ~3A - correct, and matches\nreal controllers (Kobic etc). Replaces the retired voltage follower (TIP122)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "45aaad5e-b0e7-42e9-8758-9db87929413d")
	)
	(text "SAFETY:\nShoot-through protection - if brake (Q2) and anti-brake fault on together, the\ncurrent source caps its contribution at ~3A instead of feeding a near-short.\nAdd open/short detection on the loop + fast OCP to guard source component failure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 165 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7ef2709d-0049-4617-be61-985d06dd4352")
	)
	(text "level shift + PWM->DC filter\n2N2222 + 470n + 10k/1k\n(KA_PWM_DEMAND from MCU 50kHz)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120 134 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "90085e48-a5f5-4534-87bd-2d5662fa3aad")
	)
	(text "Rsense\n0.1 ohm\n(WHITE leg)\n0.3V at 3A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 176 106 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9d65e621-2309-472b-a10f-e6e8ab476c8a")
	)
	(text "OP-AMP SUPPLY - CRITICAL:\nGD1 is powered from the WHITE rail (~16V), NOT +5V. Rsense is in the WHITE leg,\nso the op-amp inputs/output sit at ~16V common mode; a 5V op-amp cannot work here.\nUse a single-supply HV op-amp (LM321/LM358-class, >=16V, ideally 36V), GND-to-WHITE.\nConfirmed by the SIMetrix design (op-amp V+ = supply rail). Only GD2 (brake) is on +5V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 150 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a12bb87a-57fb-49b3-b20e-b8e273f47ca8")
	)
	(text "THERMAL (steady-state baseline, from SIMetrix design):\nVsupply max 16V, Ta 30C. At 2.75A -> Pd 44W (47W at full 3A).\nTIP147: SOA 125W@25C, Tj allow 125C, Rthjc 1C/W -> Rthca 1.16C/W, Tc 81C.\nSUP70060E: SOA 200W, Tj 150C, Rthjc 0.75 -> Rthca 1.98C/W, Tc 117C (smaller sink, hotter).\nAnti-brake is bursty: size heatsink by pulse energy / thermal capacitance\n(dT ~= Energy/Cth) not steady 47W - a ~50g Al sink (Cth ~45 J/C) rises ~2C per 2s burst."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 132 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ed367132-b1e4-4953-95d7-300b78618f4a")
	)
